1
00:00:00,216 --> 00:00:02,836
In a survey before Double 11

2
00:00:02,956 --> 00:00:04,226
of 1000 respondents

3
00:00:04,276 --> 00:00:08,156
66.7% said they use AI to help them shop

4
00:00:08,206 --> 00:00:10,973
comparing prices, working out discounts, bundling orders

5
00:00:11,023 --> 00:00:14,013
and finding the best combination of coupons

6
00:00:14,221 --> 00:00:18,698
And 85.7% feel AI makes shopping easier

7
00:00:18,748 --> 00:00:20,881
cheaper, and less of a headache

8
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,410
But a Dazhong News reporter put one question to the test

9
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:27,504
checking out exactly the way AI said was best

10
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:29,514
Three orders, and not one of them matched

11
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,300
Even which platform was cheapest came out backwards

12
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:33,796
My first reaction was

13
00:00:33,846 --> 00:00:35,346
can AI get the math wrong too

14
00:00:35,536 --> 00:00:38,626
Doesn't it read through every platform's rules

15
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:40,320
Don't rush to uninstall it just yet

16
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,845
Where it goes wrong is in the things it can't see

17
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,882
And those are the things that really cost you

18
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:46,382
This is Pixel Breath

19
00:00:46,452 --> 00:00:50,312
Today, let's talk about why AI's discount math doesn't add up

20
00:00:51,216 --> 00:00:53,227
So why do we think AI reads everything

21
00:00:53,487 --> 00:00:55,559
Where does that impression come from

22
00:00:55,609 --> 00:00:59,029
Deposit discounts, store coupons, cross-store deals

23
00:00:59,289 --> 00:01:01,579
88VIP, red packets, and national subsidies

24
00:01:01,909 --> 00:01:03,439
Rules stacked on rules

25
00:01:03,589 --> 00:01:06,020
In past years, bundling orders felt like solving a math olympiad problem

26
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:09,230
To hit a discount threshold, you'd add things you didn't need yet

27
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:12,860
This year, lots of people are handing the math over to AI

28
00:01:12,942 --> 00:01:15,812
And platforms are putting AI shopping assistants front and center

29
00:01:15,925 --> 00:01:17,705
Taobao's homepage now has Qwen built in

30
00:01:17,762 --> 00:01:20,352
Link your account, grab coupons and order right there

31
00:01:20,632 --> 00:01:23,922
JD has Dongdong, and Doubao launched a shopping section

32
00:01:23,986 --> 00:01:25,366
And the scale has grown too

33
00:01:25,696 --> 00:01:26,979
Taobao says its AI search

34
00:01:27,029 --> 00:01:30,066
has handled nearly 50 million shopping requests

35
00:01:30,203 --> 00:01:33,763
JD's AI usage is up 3.2 times over the 618 sale

36
00:01:33,832 --> 00:01:35,192
And AI really is fast

37
00:01:35,256 --> 00:01:38,476
A Jinhua Evening News reporter tested it on a Sony lens

38
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:39,572
Doing the math by hand

39
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:42,842
it came to 1349 yuan on JD

40
00:01:43,132 --> 00:01:45,232
and 1358 on Taobao

41
00:01:45,522 --> 00:01:49,482
In seconds, AI found a way to get it for 1215 yuan

42
00:01:49,545 --> 00:01:51,625
Official discounts, member discounts

43
00:01:51,675 --> 00:01:53,815
and Taobao coins, all stacked together

44
00:01:53,871 --> 00:01:56,641
But fast doesn't mean right

45
00:01:56,696 --> 00:01:59,836
A shopper named Xiao Zhou gave AI all the rules for a whole order

46
00:01:59,901 --> 00:02:02,231
and checked out following its plan to split the order

47
00:02:02,284 --> 00:02:04,453
only to find two of the coupons were mutually exclusive

48
00:02:04,503 --> 00:02:06,320
and couldn't be stacked at all

49
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,800
Others ran into last-minute price hikes

50
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:10,740
or big coupons pulled back by the platform

51
00:02:10,808 --> 00:02:12,945
In the coupon plans AI gave

52
00:02:12,995 --> 00:02:14,585
none of this was mentioned

53
00:02:14,865 --> 00:02:16,665
But here's what I think

54
00:02:16,715 --> 00:02:18,285
AI didn't get the math wrong

55
00:02:18,425 --> 00:02:20,595
It just can't see certain things

56
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:22,557
So those three orders from the reporter

57
00:02:22,607 --> 00:02:24,227
where exactly did AI go wrong

58
00:02:25,139 --> 00:02:27,849
An experiment Dazhong News ran on November 13

59
00:02:27,902 --> 00:02:30,792
Buy a phone plus a gift box of liquor

60
00:02:31,102 --> 00:02:33,002
in one combined order on the same platform

61
00:02:33,052 --> 00:02:35,392
and have AI stack the coupons platform by platform

62
00:02:35,462 --> 00:02:36,962
to work out the final price

63
00:02:37,019 --> 00:02:40,239
AI's answer: 7769 yuan on Douyin

64
00:02:40,509 --> 00:02:42,549
7822 on JD

65
00:02:42,789 --> 00:02:45,049
and 8110 on Tmall

66
00:02:45,379 --> 00:02:49,103
Douyin was cheapest, with a 340-yuan spread across the three

67
00:02:49,153 --> 00:02:51,894
Then the reporter opened the official flagship stores on all three

68
00:02:51,944 --> 00:02:54,424
added the same items to the cart

69
00:02:54,544 --> 00:02:56,454
and checked every coupon one by one

70
00:02:56,754 --> 00:02:58,844
member discounts, platform subsidies

71
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:01,617
At the submit-order step, they looked at the actual total

72
00:03:01,857 --> 00:03:04,567
Douyin came to 9398 yuan

73
00:03:04,831 --> 00:03:07,051
JD only 8620

74
00:03:07,104 --> 00:03:09,674
and Tmall 8885

75
00:03:10,074 --> 00:03:15,284
The three orders were off by 1629, 798 and 775 yuan

76
00:03:15,353 --> 00:03:16,553
The ranking flipped too

77
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:19,411
Douyin, which AI called the cheapest, was actually the most expensive

78
00:03:19,461 --> 00:03:21,321
So where's the gap

79
00:03:21,511 --> 00:03:24,951
What AI can read are the rules written on the page

80
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:27,861
what a coupon takes off once you spend enough

81
00:03:27,911 --> 00:03:29,141
and where the threshold is

82
00:03:29,291 --> 00:03:32,002
But what really decides the final price is your logged-in account

83
00:03:32,052 --> 00:03:34,066
and what you only see at the very last step

84
00:03:34,116 --> 00:03:37,931
whether this coupon and that one cancel each other out

85
00:03:38,211 --> 00:03:40,291
that this coupon already ran out today

86
00:03:40,341 --> 00:03:42,821
that this price changed five minutes ago

87
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,399
Here's information asymmetry in plain terms

88
00:03:44,449 --> 00:03:48,069
The seller holds the cards, and the buyer can't see them

89
00:03:48,339 --> 00:03:50,100
AI is on the buyer's side

90
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:53,430
but what it reads is the half the seller chose to show

91
00:03:53,510 --> 00:03:56,000
As the saying goes, the buyer is never as sharp as the seller

92
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:58,030
and AI can't close that gap for you either

93
00:03:58,133 --> 00:04:00,633
Worse, that table looks too tidy

94
00:04:00,733 --> 00:04:03,281
A few seconds, three rows of numbers, one best option

95
00:04:03,331 --> 00:04:07,241
Back when you couldn't work it out, you'd go to the last step and check yourself

96
00:04:07,461 --> 00:04:08,669
Now that AI has done the math for you

97
00:04:08,719 --> 00:04:11,661
you might not even open the checkout page

98
00:04:11,723 --> 00:04:14,973
AI hasn't actually eliminated the information gap

99
00:04:15,173 --> 00:04:18,663
It's just wrapped it up to look certain

100
00:04:19,012 --> 00:04:21,562
So can you still use that table

101
00:04:22,481 --> 00:04:23,661
First, a caveat

102
00:04:23,711 --> 00:04:25,111
AI isn't useless

103
00:04:25,481 --> 00:04:27,951
It handles the public rules fast and thoroughly

104
00:04:28,261 --> 00:04:31,201
That 1215-yuan route really exists

105
00:04:31,551 --> 00:04:33,831
and the time it saves you is real

106
00:04:33,916 --> 00:04:36,719
It just can't fill in the half the platform keeps hidden

107
00:04:36,769 --> 00:04:39,659
So there's only one way to use it: treat AI as a draft

108
00:04:39,709 --> 00:04:40,879
not the final price

109
00:04:41,299 --> 00:04:42,735
Let it give you options

110
00:04:42,785 --> 00:04:44,820
and a ceiling. Before you buy

111
00:04:44,870 --> 00:04:46,700
go to the submit-order step yourself

112
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:48,430
and look at the checkout preview

113
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:50,970
The price at that step is the real one

114
00:04:51,036 --> 00:04:52,126
The way I see it

115
00:04:52,186 --> 00:04:55,316
AI can help us compare prices across platforms

116
00:04:55,369 --> 00:04:58,048
but don't let it take the last step for you

117
00:04:58,098 --> 00:05:01,438
The half it can't see yet, we have to walk through ourselves

118
00:05:01,534 --> 00:05:03,124
Back to those three orders from the start

119
00:05:03,174 --> 00:05:04,954
What's missing isn't AI's intelligence

120
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,990
It's that AI, just like the user

121
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,620
can't see the card in the seller's hand

122
00:05:09,686 --> 00:05:13,466
Go all the way to the checkout page, and you'll dodge the coupon traps

123
00:05:13,518 --> 00:05:16,538
So what if we hand that last step to AI too

124
00:05:16,848 --> 00:05:18,678
Have it place the order and pay for you

125
00:05:18,938 --> 00:05:22,527
In early November, United Airlines started keeping AI assistants

126
00:05:22,577 --> 00:05:24,237
out of its booking system

127
00:05:24,454 --> 00:05:25,802
Next time, let's talk about

128
00:05:25,852 --> 00:05:29,704
whether AI can make that final payment for you
